.th BANNER VI 23/8/77
.sh NAME
banner \*- make a banner
.sh SYNOPSIS
.it banner
[ - ] [ "string" ... ]
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it banner
transforms its arguments into banner lines on the standard output.
If the first argument is '-' it assumes 124 cols, otherwise 80.
If there are no other arguments, 
.it banner
reads from its standard input.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
.it ptbanner
(VI),
.it message
(VI)
.sh AUTHOR
Piers Lauder (\ University of Sydney\ )
.sh BUGS
Sparse 64 character set.
